# An immutable container remains immutable even if it (preference)

Standing user preference: An immutable container remains immutable even if it holds a reference to a mutable object whose value later changes; immutability applies to the set of contained objects, not their internal state.

## Conventions
- An immutable container remains immutable even if it holds a reference to a mutable object whose value later changes; immutability applies to the set of contained objects, not their internal state.

